{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Bhaddaji","html":"<article id='thag2.22'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.22 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.22 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Tatiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Three </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Bhaddajittheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Bhaddaji </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Panādo nāma so rājā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>There was a king named Panāda </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yassa yūpo suvaṇṇayo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who had a sacrificial post all golden. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tiriyaṁ soḷasubbedho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Its height was sixteen times its width, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ubbhamāhu sahassadhā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and the top was a thousandfold. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sahassakaṇḍo satageṇḍu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>It had a thousand panels and a hundred ball-caps, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dhajālu haritāmayo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>all adorned with banners, and made of sun gold. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Anaccuṁ tattha gandhabbā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>There danced the centaurs, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>chasahassāni sattadhā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>numbering seven times six thousand. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Bhaddajitthero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
